Done. Here's a summary of the change:

**What changed:** `src/prompt.rs`

**Implementation:** At the `ModelCallCompleted` "completed" call site (line ~962, the normal completion path), the `error_detail` parameter was changed from `None` to a conditional: when `state.usage.input == 0 && state.usage.output == 0`, it now passes `Some("model returned zero tokens — possible API error, timeout, or empty response")`. Non-zero-token completions are unchanged.

**Tests added:**
• `model_call_terminal_payload_zero_tokens_completed_includes_error_detail` — verifies that a completed call with 0/0 tokens includes `error_detail` containing "zero tokens"
• `model_call_terminal_payload_nonzero_tokens_no_error_detail` — verifies no regression: non-zero-token completions don't get an `error_detail`

**Verification:** `cargo fmt -- --check` (pass), `cargo build` (pass), `cargo test prompt` (321+6 pass), specific test run (3/3 pass).

**Why this matters:** When a session fails silently because the model returned zero tokens, future state traces will include `error_detail` explaining the likely cause, making the `deepseek_model_call_abnormal_completed_count` metric actionable instead of opaque.

